  "adaptations": [
    "Retain upstream text/selection event-count synchronization, shared TextInputState registration, ref methods, accessibility mapping and native commands while substituting a distinct native component identity.",
    "Reuse the pinned platform shadow nodes, props, state, event emitters, measurement and adoption logic through explicit custom descriptor registration.",
    "Android inherits the stock text-input manager and editor. Its InputConnection wrapper observes explicit backward-delete operations against pre-edit native text; empty commitText/setComposingText calls remain ordinary editing.",
    "UIKit retains the full pinned component-view implementation and observes public deleteBackward on managed backed controls. No private UIKit selector or global framework patch is introduced.",
    "The adapter requires the exact reviewed React Native JS/native baseline. Native builds validate source fingerprints and the lazy runtime rejects missing hosts or a version mismatch with rebuild guidance.",
    "Android preserves the current empty Editable for a one-shot, counter-exact acknowledgement of an owned native deletion when only text, acknowledgement count or accessibility state changes and all own plain-text base attributes and paragraph metadata match. Rich, attachment, unknown or oversized metadata uses the stock path. The native edit already refreshed its span cache. Explicit commands, composition, batching, layout/editing changes and retired ownership retain the stock update path. This deliberately avoids an unnecessary empty-buffer reset and preserves its native undo state.",
    "UIKit backed editor replacements retain authored accessibility identifiers, labels, hints, language, visibility, traits and explicit values when unchanged React props are not replayed. Derived editor text values remain native."
  ]
